      "notes": [
        {
          "category": "summary",
          "text": "An update for apache-commons-beanutils is now available for Red Hat Enterprise Linux 9.4 Extended Update Support.\n\nRed Hat Product Security has rated this update as having a security impact of Important. A Common Vulnerability Scoring System (CVSS) base score, which gives a detailed severity rating, is available for each vulnerability from the CVE link(s) in the References section.",
          "title": "Topic"
        },
        {
          "category": "general",
          "text": "The Apache Commons BeanUtils library provides utility methods for accessing and modifying properties of arbitrary JavaBeans.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* commons-beanutils: Apache Commons BeanUtils: PropertyUtilsBean does not suppresses an enum's declaredClass property by default (CVE-2025-48734)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.",
          "title": "Details"
        },
